# Keeps the ADA_ECU/ build context small. The Dockerfile's stage boundaries decide what lands
# in the image - this file only stops useless bytes being uploaded to the builder.
#
# Do NOT add tests/ here: stage 1 needs it at CONFIGURE time (CMakeLists.txt names
# tests/**.cpp in ada_add_test()'s add_executable(), and CMake errors on a missing source file
# even for targets the image build never compiles). tests/ is build-stage only and never
# reaches the runtime stage.
#
# Do NOT add media/ itself: media/ego-b-occluding-c.mp4 is the R12 clip the runtime stage
# gains in Phase 3 (12.3.7.2). Only its provenance notes are excluded below.

# A local developer build tree - _deps alone holds the FetchContent clones plus their object
# files, i.e. useless megabytes of context.
build/

# Documentation is never part of the image (node-code-layout.md: doc/ is documentation only);
# README.md is the folder's human guide, same category.
doc/
README.md

# Host-side test equipment - never deployed, never in the image.
tools/

# The schema authority copy for the CRA assessment record - a doc/contract artifact, not a
# runtime input.
schema/

# Test tooling manifest (pytest etc.). The runtime manifest is detector/requirements.txt,
# which arrives with the detector in Phase 3.
detector/requirements-dev.txt

# Clip provenance, not clip data - the mp4 stays in the context (see header). Both patterns:
# the committed note is media/ego-b-occluding-c.source.md; media/source/ covers a future
# provenance folder.
media/source/
media/*.source.md

# Python bytecode from local detector/tools runs - stale and platform-specific.
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
